## V14 complete: UI-task model routing to the strongest servable model, plus the joined design pipeline

Committed as `6f53661` (feature) and `4d359f4` (regression fixes) on `khamis1992/v0-v14`.
Acceptance criterion: *the e2e run scores above the baseline on the V1 eval set* - met:
`baseline mean 97.8 -> pipeline mean 98.2 (delta +0.4)`, `improved 2/12, regressed 0`.

### What shipped

**1. Routing (`src/models/route.ts`, new, model-free)**

`routeUiModel(config)` decides which model serves a UI task. The rule under test is
the negative one: a model id with no live provider is not a stronger choice, it is a
model that cannot be served.

- Takes the first entry of the coding chain that a provider can actually serve, then
  falls back to the strongest usable provider when the chain is empty, then to the
  configured model, then to a local model.
- "Usable" means enabled, credentialed, and not in cooldown. A chain entry naming a
  model nothing serves is skipped, never chosen.
- Every decision carries its `source` (`coding` | `strongest` | `default`) so a
  caller can tell a real route from a fallback.
- The chosen model's provider chain is ordered strongest-first, so failover follows
  the same strength order the route used.

**2. The joined pipeline (`src/design/pipeline.ts`, new, ~1000 lines)**

One bounded run: classify -> brief -> examples -> scaffold -> generate -> autofix ->
build (max 3) -> screenshot -> critique (max 2) -> score.

- Every effect is injected (model, linter, critique, generator, scorer), so the loop
  is assertable offline and no network is touched in tests.
- The baseline comparison is honest: `improved` means the final score beats the score
  of the *same workspace before the pipeline ran*, not a hard-coded number.
- Generated output is capped at a file budget, with the truncation reported as a note.
- RTL is a first-class path: the generator emits `dir="rtl"`, Arabic `lang`, and
  logical properties (`margin-inline`, `padding-inline`) instead of physical ones.

**3. Linter correctness (`src/design/tokenLint.ts`)**

- Guarded the `left-`/`right-` utility regexes so prose like "right-to-left" is no
  longer matched as the class `right-1`. The first attempt still matched prose via a
  second alternative, so the guard is now `(?:^|[\s"'`])right-(?![a-z])`.
- Folded the RTL rules into one per-site pass (`foldRtlIssues`) with `isUiSource` to
  exclude build tooling, so a stylesheet is never told it is "missing `dir=rtl`".
- Made `rtlReady` direction-aware: an RTL request needs a declared direction *and*
  logical properties; an LTR request needs the document not to declare the other
  direction. The fold and the metric share the same helpers, so they cannot drift.

**4. The gate (`src/scripts/check-design-pipeline.ts`, new)**

Runs every V1 fixture twice through the *same* scorer (`scoreFixture` from
`eval-design.ts`) and the *same* linter, with a mock model client that never opens a
socket. The baseline is a deliberately weak brief (`baselineBrief`) standing for
"the brief stage never ran" - still schema-valid and locale-correct, so an RTL
baseline cannot fail on a technicality. Both sides run a real build through the
scaffold's own `build.mjs`. The gate fails when anything regresses.

### Acceptance criteria (from `.jtask.md`)

| Requirement | Where asserted |
| --- | --- |
| UI tasks route to the strongest available model | `src/models/__tests__/route.test.ts` (16 tests): chain preference, skipping an unservable entry, disabled/missing-key/cooldown exclusion, strongest-provider fallback, and the `source` on every decision |
| e2e run scores above the baseline on the V1 eval set | `src/scripts/__tests__/check-design-pipeline.test.ts` (10 tests) plus the CLI: `delta +0.4`, `regressed 0`, and a test that asserts `passed === notWorse` |
| pipeline stages actually run, in order | `pipeline.test.ts` "runs every stage once, in pipeline order" and the gate test that requires all nine stage names in every report |
| bounded loops | build <= 3 and critique <= 2 asserted through `result.stages`, including a `maxCritiqueRounds: 0` case |
| RTL quality | `evalDesign.test.ts` RTL cases plus `pipeline.test.ts` "renders an RTL document with a logical-property layout" |

### Gates (all run from the worktree root)

| Gate | Command | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| root types | `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |
| server build | `npm run build:server` | exit 0 (server bundle + pdf worker written to `dist/`) |
| web build | `cd packages/web && npx next build` | exit 0 (compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages) |
| encoding | `npm run check:encoding` | OK (no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid) |
| new + touched suites | `node --import tsx --test "src/design/__tests__/*.test.ts" src/models/__tests__/route.test.ts src/scripts/__tests__/check-design-pipeline.test.ts` | 248 tests, 248 pass, 0 fail |
| e2e gate | `npm run check:design-pipeline` | delta +0.4, 0 regressed, exit 0 |

### Three defects found by running the gates rather than trusting a green test run

1. **`rtlReady` became unconditional.** Folding the RTL rules per site made the metric
   require `dir="rtl"` plus logical properties for every page, so a clean
   left-to-right site reported `rtlReady: false` and `evalDesign.test.ts` failed
   14/15. Fixed by making the metric direction-aware; the fold and the metric now
   share `declaresDirRtl` / `usesLogicalProperties` so they cannot drift.
2. **`createPipelineWorkspace` assumed its root exists.** `mkdtemp` only creates the
   leaf, so the gate died with `ENOENT ... out\loam-design-pipeline-XXXXXX` on a clean
   checkout where `out/` does not exist. The root is now created first, with a
   regression test for a nested missing root.
3. **An explicitly empty `fixtures: []` was treated as "all fixtures".** A scoped run
   silently became a full-set run. The gate now distinguishes `undefined` (all) from
   `[]` (none).

### Rules honoured

- Only the files listed below were added or changed. No `.cc-*` marker file was
  committed. `.jdone` / `.jcode-done` stay tracked as the append-only rollups they
  are (`.gitattributes` declares `merge=union`), and this report is prepended to the
  preserved rollup rather than replacing it.
- No forbidden path touched (`docs/handoff/watchdog.ps1`, `qa/*.png`,
  `packages/tests/visual/baselines`, ZCode/Codex files).
- No real external model API was called: the gate and every test use in-process fakes.
- No secrets committed, nothing pushed, no `git reset --hard`, no discarded work.
- All file content was written with the file tools (`write` / `edit` / `apply_patch`);
  the shell ran commands only. No Arabic text was written by this session, so no
  mojibake was introduced.
- The temp probe `scripts/tmp-lint-rtl.ts` was deleted before the first commit.
- Techniques were learned from `.cc-ref/V0_RE.md`; all rules, prompts and tool
  descriptions are written in Loam's own words. No v0/Vercel prompt text was copied.

### Files

- `src/models/route.ts` (new) + `src/models/__tests__/route.test.ts` (new)
- `src/design/pipeline.ts` (new) + `src/design/__tests__/pipeline.test.ts` (new)
- `src/design/tokenLint.ts` (modified)
- `src/scripts/check-design-pipeline.ts` (new) + `src/scripts/__tests__/check-design-pipeline.test.ts` (new)
- `package.json` (`check:design-pipeline`, `test:design-pipeline`)

### Seams left for other workstreams

- **V13 (quick-edit route):** this router is UI-task-only today. The quick-edit
  classifier can reuse `routeUiModel` for its "fast model for narrow edits" half, but
  the narrow/broad edit decision is not wired into the route.
- **Registry wiring:** the pipeline calls `searchDesignBlocks` for the examples stage;
  a new block category needs no pipeline change, only a manifest entry.
- **Screenshot stage:** the capture itself remains the caller's browser effect; the
  pipeline records the stage and reports what the build state allows.
- **Arabic/RTL copy:** the generator emits `dir="rtl"` and logical properties, but the
  generated prose is English unless a fixture supplies copy; no locale catalog was
  touched by this task.

### Test commands

```
npx tsc --noEmit
npm run build:server
cd packages/web && npx next build
npm run check:encoding
npm run check:design-pipeline
node --import tsx --test "src/design/__tests__/*.test.ts" src/models/__tests__/route.test.ts src/scripts/__tests__/check-design-pipeline.test.ts
```

