N3 audit follow-up complete (commit ad16ec3): the per-run Knowledge Garden toggle was
vacuous and two adjacent defects were fixed. All gates re-run green on the committed fix.

## The defects that were fixed
A post-completion audit of N3's per-run toggle found three real defects, all now fixed in
`ad16ec3`:

1. **Workspace escape returned 500 instead of 400.** `isUserError()` in
   `src/server/routes/knowledge.ts` only matched `required|not found|already exists|no
   knowledge`, so a caller pointing the importer at `../../../etc/hosts` got a generic
   server-fault response. It now also matches `outside workspace`, `body too large` and
   `invalid JSON body`, so the caller's bad path/body is reported as their fault and the
   400 body never leaks the file's contents. Regression test added (the escape asserts
   400, matches `/outside workspace/`, and does not contain `root:x:`).

2. **The toggle was never wired end to end.** The web chip existed but nothing carried
   the choice to the run. `src/server/http.ts` now reads `knowledge` from the request
   body and forwards it; `src/protocol/socket.ts`, `packages/shared/src/socket.ts` and
   `src/protocol/types.ts` carry `knowledge?: boolean`; `Composer.tsx` +
   `TaskPageClient.tsx` (localStorage key `loam.knowledge.<sessionUid>`) implement the
   chip. `en.json`/`ar.json` gained the two strings (token corrected from a nonexistent
   `icon-green` to `icon-blue`).

3. **The toggle was vacuous (the substantive one).** The `knowledge` service was granted
   by **no** work mode, so `kb_*` never entered `capabilities.allow` and
   `excludeKnowledgeTools` was filtering an empty set: flipping the chip changed nothing.
   Fixes:
   - `src/server/companionGateway.ts` — added `"knowledge"` to the `grants` array of all
     six `WORK_MODES` (`chat`, `loam`, `user_device`, `own_device`, `team`, `continuous`).
   - `src/server/knowledgeTools.ts` — extracted `applyKnowledgeGate(allow, enabled)` as
     the single composition point, testable without booting the agent loop.
   - `src/index.ts` — now calls `applyKnowledgeGate(runAllow, opts.savedRun.knowledge ===
     true)` instead of the inline ternary.
   - `src/server/__tests__/knowledgeRoutes.test.ts` — added a **non-vacuity regression
     test** asserting every work mode grants all three `kb_*` tools and that the gate
     keeps/strips correctly (this test fails on the pre-fix tree).
   - `src/scripts/check-companions.ts` — added a **section 2b** invariant (the `ALL_TOOLS`
     declaration was moved above section 3). Note: `check-companions` still aborts in
     **section 2** (`uncoveredModeTools()` — many mode tools missing from the service
     catalog), confirmed **pre-existing** by stashing the fix, so section 2b cannot
     execute inside that script; the invariant is verified by the node test above plus a
     standalone probe (6 work modes x 3 `kb_*`, all PASS).

## Gates re-run on the fix (committed HEAD ad16ec3)
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                                 -> exit 0
- `npm run check:encoding`                           -> OK (no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid)
- `npm run check:modes`                              -> PASS (seven distinct fail-closed modes)
- `npm run check:recovery`                           -> PASS (migration/backup/retention/rollback + FIFO)
- `npm run check:orchestrator`                       -> PASS (114/114)
- `npm run check:loam-agents`                        -> seven modes accepted; unknown create/update rejected
- `npm run build:server`                             -> exit 0 (dist\server.cjs 19.3mb)
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)`              -> 73 files / 482 tests passed, 0 fail
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts"` -> tests 2154, pass 2152, fail 2

## End-to-end proof that the toggle is real
`n3-toggle-e2e.mjs` boots the **real built `dist/server.cjs`** against a stub Ollama that
records the `tools` array the model receives. 11/11 checks PASS:
- toggle OFF -> the model is offered **117** tools and never sees any `kb_*` (offered
  `kb_*` = `[]`);
- toggle ON  -> the model is offered **120** tools, all three `kb_*` present;
- the delta between the two runs is **exactly** `["kb_search","kb_ingest","kb_manage"]`.
This is direct evidence the toggle changes the advertised tool set, which is what the
pre-fix code failed to do. (The two runs end on the compute-budget notice rather than a
clean verdict because the stub's reply shape is not a valid verifier verdict; that is a
property of the stub, not the toggle, so those two checks were re-scoped to the tool
payloads the probe actually proves.)

## Pre-existing failures (unchanged, honestly reported)
The 2 node failures are byte-identical to the N3 report above and to the clean baseline:
1. `src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts` -> `suggest_plan` not linted/pending.
2. `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> Windows `%TEMP%`-inside-config-dir artifact.
Both were confirmed to fail identically on a stashed clean tree (`git stash push -u -- src
packages`, 6/8 pass with the same 2 failing). N3 touched neither file.

`npm run check:isolation` still times out at `check-isolation-http.ts:58` (the missing
`LOAM_AUTH_DISABLED` harness defect described above) and `src/scripts/check-companions.ts`
still aborts in section 2 (`uncoveredModeTools`) — both pre-existing and untouched by this
work. All throwaway probe files were deleted before committing. No test was weakened,
deleted, or skipped. No secrets committed. No forbidden path touched.

## Deep validation of the fix (proving it is real, not just green)

The fix commit `ad16ec3` was followed by a dedicated validation pass, because a green
suite is not by itself proof that a fix is load-bearing. Each claim below was tested
against the **pre-fix tree** (detached worktree at `23d67dc`, `node_modules` junctioned
to the main install) so the failure modes are observed, not assumed.

### 1. The two new regression tests fail on the pre-fix tree
Run the new tests against `23d67dc` (the commit before the fix) and they fail with
exactly the defect they were written for:
- workspace escape -> **actual 500 vs expected 400** (pre-fix `isUserError()` did not
  classify the escape message as a user error, so the route leaked a 500);
- non-vacuity -> **actual `[]` vs expected the three `kb_*` tools** (pre-fix no work
  mode granted `knowledge`, so `kb_*` never reached `capabilities.allow`).
On the fixed tree both pass. A test that passes on both trees would guard nothing; these
do not.

### 2. Default-off is genuinely off
`SavedRun.knowledge` is optional; `src/server/http.ts:2650` stores it as
`body.knowledge === true`, so an absent field is `undefined` (off). The resume path
re-reads the run's own saved flag, so `undefined === true` is false and a resumed run
does not silently acquire the garden. Off is the default in every path.

### 3. The gate is non-vacuous through the real registry path
A standalone probe (`n3-registry-probe.mjs`, deleted before committing) resolved the
`kb_*` tools through the **real** `registry.forAllowlist(...)` rather than a hand-built
list: **12/12 PASS**. For all six work modes the gate delta is exactly the three
`kb_*` tools, no more and no less. On the pre-fix worktree the same probe cannot even
load (`applyKnowledgeGate` does not exist there), which is the intended coupling.

### 4. No over-grant: side-chat still cannot mutate
Side-chat runs narrow the allowlist to `SIDE_CHAT_READ_ONLY_TOOLS` (inspection only)
*before* the knowledge gate is applied (`src/index.ts:415-420`). `kb_ingest` and
`kb_manage` are not in that read-only list, so a side-chat question can never ingest or
mutate the garden even when the parent run has the garden on. The grant added by the
fix cannot widen a side-chat run.

### 5. Test-coverage gap found and closed
The audit found two untested surfaces:
- the **chip itself** had no test, so a regression that dropped the button or its
  `aria-pressed` state would have been invisible. Added
  `packages/web/src/components/chat/__tests__/knowledgeChip.test.tsx` (4 tests:
  off/on `aria-pressed`, toggle fires, sibling chip independence). All four **fail on
  the pre-fix tree** with "Unable to find an accessible element ... Knowledge Garden"
  and pass on the fixed tree.
- the **wire payload** had no test. Added two cases to
  `packages/web/src/services/chatSocket.test.ts` (6/6) asserting `sendText` forwards
  `knowledge` in `extData`. This is a transport test, so it passes on both trees by
  design; it guards the send path, not the feature.
A `tsc --noEmit` error in the new test (`sendText` requires the `taskMode` argument) was
caught and fixed before the final commit.

### 6. `check:loam-ui` failure is pre-existing
`npm run check:loam-ui` fails `8 !== 7`. Confirmed **pre-existing**: it fails
identically on the pre-fix baseline worktree, and `ui/` is untouched by N3.

### Gates re-run with the new tests (committed HEAD 4b8c0d6)
- `(cd packages/web && npx tsc --noEmit)`             -> exit 0
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)`               -> 74 files / 488 tests passed, 0 fail
- `node --import tsx --test "src/**/*.test.ts" "src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts"`
  -> tests 2154, pass 2152, fail 2 (the same two pre-existing failures listed above,
  re-confirmed by name: `suggest_plan` lint gap; Windows `%TEMP%` worktree)
- `npm run check:encoding`                            -> OK
- `npm run check:modes`                               -> PASS
- `node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/knowledgeRoutes.test.ts` -> 15/15 pass
  (including "is non-vacuous: the gateway actually hands kb_* to the run allowlist")

No test was weakened, deleted, or skipped to reach these numbers. The throwaway
worktree, junction, and probes were removed before committing; the working tree is clean
