`src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` -> "reports non-git folders without
throwing" (`true == false` at `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts:44`).
Neither `src/server/__tests__/worktrees.test.ts` nor `src/server/worktrees.ts`
is touched by this merge (`git diff` of both between the pre-merge HEAD and the
merged HEAD is empty), and the cause is environmental: `%TEMP%` on this machine is
`C:\Users\khamis\AppData\Local\Temp`, and `git -C %TEMP% rev-parse` walks up and
resolves to `C:/Users/khamis`, which is itself a git repository, so a fresh temp
folder is reported as a git folder. Confirmed by a direct probe in this session.

