| Gate | Command | Result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| --- | --- | --- |
| root types | `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |
| root types | `npx tsc --noEmit` | exit 0 |
| server build | `npm run build:server` | exit 0 (`dist/server.cjs 19.6mb`, pdf worker copied) |
| web build | `cd packages/web && npx next build` | exit 0 (compiled successfully, 25/25 static pages) |
| touched tests | `node --import tsx --test src/agent/__tests__/fanout.test.ts src/graph/__tests__/runGraph.test.ts src/subagent/__tests__/registry.test.ts src/agent/__tests__/recipeEngine.test.ts src/tools/__tests__/workflow.test.ts src/tools/__tests__/wideResearch.test.ts` | 105 tests, 105 pass, 0 fail |
The fanout suite alone is 11 tests / 11 pass / 0 fail. No existing test was weakened,
deleted or skipped.
## Seams left for other workstreams
- **N4 (incremental Recipe):** the fan-out is a tool today. A first-class `fanout`
  recipe step that the planner can propose and the executor can restart from a branch
  node is not wired; `createBranch`/`createMerge` and the `fanout_branch` /
  `fanout_merge` events are the seam it should plug into.
- **N11 (canvas editing semantics):** branch/merge nodes are renderable and labelled but
  not yet editable/cuttable; the node types are registered in `CANVAS_NODE_TYPES` and
  `NODE_TYPE_KEYS` so the canvas work only needs the interactions.
- **N14 (share/replay):** branch/merge nodes flow through the existing export path by
  type, but no replay-specific handling was added.
- **N21 (Arabic/RTL):** labels are English only; the canvas labels live in
  `NODE_TYPE_KEYS` and the locale catalogs were not touched by this task.
- **N19 (master prompt):** the "when to fan out" guidance is not in the master prompt
  yet; the tool description carries the guidance in the meantime.
## Rules honoured
## Rules honoured
